        <h2>Splurge and Special Occasion (Over $100)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Garrison Brothers Balmorhea</strong> &mdash; bourbon aged in one new oak barrel, then moved into a second new barrel for more. Enormous: dark chocolate, molasses, black cherry, and oak for days. Not a cocktail whiskey. A porch whiskey.</li>
          <li><strong>Garrison Brothers Cowboy Bourbon</strong> &mdash; an uncut, unfiltered annual release drawn from their best barrels. Allocated and gone fast; put your name on our list.</li>
          <li><strong>Still Austin Cask Strength Bourbon</strong> &mdash; The Musician's louder sibling, bottled at barrel proof. Add a few drops of water and watch it open up.</li>
          <li><strong>Ironroot Republic single barrel releases</strong> &mdash; limited bottlings that show what one Denison barrel can do. When we have one, it's usually on the counter.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Gift Picks From Behind the Counter</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>For the Texan who moved away:</strong> Still Austin The Musician. Local, beautiful label, drinks well neat.</li>
          <li><strong>For the bourbon collector:</strong> Garrison Brothers Small Batch or, if the occasion warrants, Balmorhea.</li>
          <li><strong>For the scotch drinker:</strong> Balcones Texas Single Malt or Andalusia Stryker.</li>
          <li><strong>For the host who has everything:</strong> Ironroot Harbinger, because they almost certainly don't have it yet.</li>
        </ul>
